go 1.26.4

// The repository's Go modules, so `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` and
// `go run ./examples/...` all work from the repository root rather than from
// each module directory.
//
// Committed, unlike most workspaces. Every member is inside this repository, so
// it describes the tree rather than one machine — and a contributor who has to
// discover that the example only runs from its own directory has been given a
// puzzle instead of a repository. It carries no replace directives: a workspace
// applies the union of its members' replaces to every module in it, and one
// pointing outside the tree is what made a clean checkout fail before protokit
// published its service package.
use (
	./examples/music-go
	./plugin
	./transcode-go
)
